Four coordinated changes. Canonical rule: **routing is path-based** — `spriteSheetPath` on the config entry is the source of truth; the inventory (`SPRITE-INVENTORY.md`) maps path → metadata. No registry, no procedural fallback.

### 1. Schemas: stop rejecting `spriteSheetPath`

The strict schemas used `additionalProperties: false` but never declared the field, so valid configs were rejected and entries shipped without it.

```ts
// src/config/schemas.ts
export const ENEMY_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  properties: {
    id: { type: "string" },
    name: { type: "string" },
    hp: { type: "integer" },
    spriteSheetPath: { type: "string", minLength: 1 }, // was: absent -> rejected
  },
  required: ["id", "name", "hp", "spriteSheetPath"], // required: no silent procedural art
  additionalProperties: false,
} as const;

export const BOSS_SCHEMA = { /* same shape, plus phases, spriteSheetPath required */ } as const;
```

### 2. Routing: path-based resolver replaces the registry

Delete `sheetIdForEntity(entityId)` / `subjectForSheetId(sheetId)` and their hand-maintained registry. The resolver reads the config path and looks metadata up by path:

```ts
// src/sprites/routing.ts
export function resolveSheetForEntity(entry: EntityConfig): ResolvedSheet {
  const path = entry.spriteSheetPath;
  if (!path) {
    throw new RoutingError(
      `cannot resolve sprite for "${entry.id}": spriteSheetPath not set (procedural art disabled)`,
    );
  }
  const meta = assertRegistered(path); // throws on orphan pack
  return { entityId: entry.id, path, sheetId: meta.sheetId, subject: meta.subject, metadata: meta };
}
```

Call sites that did `sheetIdForEntity(e.id)` → `subjectForSheetId(...)` now call `resolveSheetForEntity(e)` and render from `resolved.path`/`resolved.metadata`.

### 3. Metadata: register the `dash-2.png` orphan

`sprites/dash/dash-2.png` existed on disk but had no inventory entry, so path routing could never resolve it. Register it (canonical source: `SPRITE-INVENTORY.md`):

```ts
// src/sprites/manifest.ts  (mirrors SPRITE-INVENTORY.md)
{
  sheetId: "dash-2",
  subject: "dash",
  pack: "dash",
  path: "sprites/dash/dash-2.png",
  frameWidth: 48,
  frameHeight: 48,
  frameCount: 2,
  anchorX: 0.5,
  anchorY: 0.9,
},

export function assertRegistered(path: string): SheetMetadata {
  const meta = byPath.get(path);
  if (!meta) throw new Error(`sprite pack "${path}" is not registered in SPRITE_INVENTORY`);
  return meta;
}
```

### 4. Boot: malformed pack aborts boot — no procedural fallback

Remove the `catch { renderProcedural(...) }` around pack loading. Validation (registered, on-disk, header format, frame geometry, frame count) throws; boot propagates and aborts:

```ts
// src/sprites/packs.ts
export function loadPack(path: string): LoadedPack {
  assertRegistered(path);                       // orphan -> error
  const header = readPackHeader(path);          // missing -> PackError
  if (header.format !== "png-v1") throw new PackError(...);
  const meta = assertRegistered(path);
  const frames = (header.width / meta.frameWidth) * (header.height / meta.frameHeight);
  if (!Number.isInteger(frames) || frames !== header.frameCount || frames !== meta.frameCount) {
    throw new PackError(`"${path}" frame geometry/count mismatch ...`);
  }
  return { ...header, validated: true };
}

// src/boot.ts
export function bootGame(entries: readonly EntityConfig[]): Map<string, RenderDescriptor> {
  const renderers = new Map<string, RenderDescriptor>();
  for (const entry of entries) {
    const resolved = resolveSheetForEntity(entry);   // throws -> boot aborts
    const pack = loadPack(resolved.path);            // throws -> boot aborts
    renderers.set(entry.id, renderEntity(entry, resolved, pack));
  }
  return renderers; // never partial: any failure throws
}
```

**The gap:** spec 01-core §6.2 promised `GET /api/v1/pools/:appID/status` served by `sandbox.StatusHandler`, but no handler and no route existed. The domain primitive already existed and is reused unchanged: `SandboxManager.PoolStatus(appID) (PoolStatus, error)` plus the `PoolStatus` JSON type (with `ErrPoolNotFound` sentinel). The fix is pure wiring, zero reimplementation.

**1. New `sandbox/status_handler.go`** — status mapping 200/404 `POOL_NOT_FOUND`/400/500, router-style `{"error":{"code","message"}}` envelope:

```go
var appIDRe = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$`)

// StatusHandler serves GET /api/v1/pools/{appID}/status (spec 01-core §6.2).
// 200 OK (PoolStatus JSON) | 400 BAD_REQUEST | 404 POOL_NOT_FOUND | 500 INTERNAL_ERROR
func StatusHandler(mgr SandboxManager) http.Handler {
	return http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		appID := r.PathValue("appID")
		if appID == "" || !appIDRe.MatchString(appID) {
			writeError(w, http.StatusBadRequest, "BAD_REQUEST",
				"path parameter appID must be a non-empty alphanumeric identifier")
			return
		}
		status, err := mgr.PoolStatus(appID) // existing primitive, untouched
		if err != nil {
			switch {
			case errors.Is(err, ErrPoolNotFound):
				writeError(w, http.StatusNotFound, "POOL_NOT_FOUND",
					fmt.Sprintf("no pool exists for appID %q", appID))
			default:
				writeError(w, http.StatusInternalServerError, "INTERNAL_ERROR",
					"failed to read pool status") // backend detail never leaked
			}
			return
		}
		writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, status)
	})
}

// Router-style error envelope shared with the rest of the API.
type errorEnvelope struct{ Error errorBody `json:"error"` }
type errorBody struct {
	Code    string `json:"code"`
	Message string `json:"message"`
}

func writeError(w http.ResponseWriter, code int, errCode, message string) {
	writeJSON(w, code, errorEnvelope{Error: errorBody{Code: errCode, Message: message}})
}

func writeJSON(w http.ResponseWriter, code int, v any) {
	w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json; charset=utf-8")
	w.WriteHeader(code)
	_ = json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(v)
}
```

**2. The one wiring line in `framework.go`** (Go 1.22+ method-pattern ServeMux; `{appID}` populates `r.PathValue`):

```go
mux := http.NewServeMux()

// U-GAP-005 fix: spec 01-core §6.2 promised this route; it was never wired.
mux.Handle("GET /api/v1/pools/{appID}/status", sandbox.StatusHandler(mgr))

// Existing route: /execute runs GetOrCreatePool before Acquire.
mux.Handle("POST /api/v1/execute", sandbox.ExecuteHandler(mgr))
```

The `/execute` handler already guarantees `GetOrCreatePool` runs before `Acquire` — which is exactly what makes the live E2E (below) work: the pool a request creates via `/execute` is immediately visible to the status route.

**3. `httptest` fake-manager tests** (`sandbox/status_handler_test.go`) — a `fakeManager` implements `SandboxManager` with injectable `statusErr`/`createErr`/`acquireErr` so the handler is tested against a controllable boundary, plus one live E2E test against the real in-memory manager through the exact `framework.go` wiring.

