**Root cause:** README counts were copied from the *tail* of one package's vitest run (`apps/api`: 163 tests / 16 files) instead of the aggregated workspace totals. `pnpm test` runs vitest per package, so the last summary line is just the last package, not the suite.

**Fix:** Sum per-package vitest summary lines across the whole run, then update *every* numeric reference in the README.

**Step 1 — run the full workspace suite, capturing all packages:**
```bash
pnpm -r test 2>&1 | tee /tmp/test-output.log
```

**Step 2 — `scripts/sum-vitest-counts.mjs`** (aggregates per-package `Test Files` / `Tests` lines; tolerates pnpm `pkg:` stream prefixes and `failed | passed` failure formats by reading the parenthesized total):
```js
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const lines = readFileSync(process.argv[2], 'utf8').split('\n');
let testFiles = 0, tests = 0;
const packages = new Set();
for (const line of lines) {
  const f = line.match(/(?:([\w@./-]+):\s+)?Test Files\s+(.+)$/);
  const t = line.match(/(?:([\w@./-]+):\s+)?Tests\s+(.+)$/);
  if (f) { testFiles += Number((f[2].match(/\((\d+)\)/) || [0, f[2].split(/\s/)[0]])[1]); if (f[1]) packages.add(f[1]); }
  if (t) { tests += Number((t[2].match(/\((\d+)\)/) || [0, t[2].split(/\s/)[0]])[1]); if (t[1]) packages.add(t[1]); }
  const h = line.match(/^> (.+?)@[^\s@]+ test \//);
  if (h) packages.add(h[1]);
}
console.log(`Test Files  ${testFiles}`);   // -> 48
console.log(`Tests       ${tests}`);        // -> 500
console.log(`Packages    ${packages.size}`);// -> 10
```

**Step 3 — `scripts/update-readme-counts.mjs`** rewrites all count references (`N tests across M files`, `N tests`, `N files`) in one pass:
```js
readme = readme.replace(/\d+\s+tests\s+across\s+\d+\s+files/gi, `${tests} tests across ${files} files`);
readme = readme.replace(/\b\d+\s+tests\b/gi, `${tests} tests`);
readme = readme.replace(/\b\d+\s+files\b/gi, `${files} files`);
```
Also delete the misleading "(apps/api subset shown above)" annotation — the count now covers the whole workspace, not a subset. Guard with a stale-reference grep in CI: `grep -E '163|16 files' README.md` must return nothing.

**Root cause (DOGFOOD-006):** `GET /api/v1/parent/progress` had no route — only `GET /progress/:parentId` existed, so the param-less path fell through to Express's 404 handler even for valid JWTs.

**Fix pattern** — add a token-resolved param-less alias. `getRequestedParentId()` is a shared resolver: explicit URL `:parentId` first (backwards-compat), falling back to `parentService.getProfileByUserId(user.id)` from the JWT. Route ordering matters: exact `/progress` must be registered **before** `/progress/:parentId`.

```ts
// src/routes/parent.ts
import { Router, Request, Response, NextFunction } from 'express';
import { parentService } from '../services/parentService';

export const parentRouter = Router();

interface AuthedRequest extends Request {
  user?: { id: string }; // injected by requireAuth JWT middleware
}

/** Resolve effective parentId: explicit :parentId param, else from JWT profile. */
async function getRequestedParentId(req: AuthedRequest, res: Response): Promise<string | null> {
  const paramParentId = req.params.parentId;
  if (typeof paramParentId === 'string') return paramParentId; // fallback path

  const userId = req.user?.id;
  if (!userId) {
    res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
    return null;
  }
  const profile = await parentService.getProfileByUserId(userId);
  if (!profile) {
    res.status(404).json({ error: 'No parent profile linked to this account',
                           code: 'PARENT_PROFILE_NOT_FOUND' });
    return null;
  }
  return profile.id;
}

// ── ORDER MATTERS: exact route FIRST, then :parentId ──────────────────────
// GET /api/v1/parent/progress — token-resolved alias (the fix)
parentRouter.get('/progress', async (req: AuthedRequest, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
  try {
    const parentId = await getRequestedParentId(req, res);
    if (!parentId) return;
    res.json({ data: await parentService.getProgress(parentId) });
  } catch (err) { next(err); }
});

// GET /api/v1/parent/progress/:parentId — explicit id (stays AFTER /progress)
parentRouter.get('/progress/:parentId', async (req: AuthedRequest, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
  try {
    res.json({ data: await parentService.getProgress(
      typeof req.params.parentId === 'string' ? req.params.parentId : '') });
  } catch (err) { next(err); }
});
```

