### Fix 2 — Seed the dev-JWT user row (the 503 is a masked FK violation)

`POST /trees` inserts the tree **and** a `tree_members` row whose `user_id` comes from the JWT `sub`. Local PG has no such `users` row, so the insert hits FK `23503` on `tree_members.user_id → users.id`, which the API currently reports as 503 "database unavailable". Fix by seeding the dev user (or point `DATABASE_URL` at the compose PG whose init scripts already seed it):

```sql
-- e2e/seed-dev-user.sql
-- The dev JWT's `sub` MUST exist in users, or tree creation fails the
-- tree_members FK constraint (SQLSTATE 23503).
INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at, updated_at)
VALUES (
  '00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000d3b4',  -- == dev JWT sub
  'dev@canopy.local',
  'Canopy Dev',
  now(), now()
)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
